shallow and buyers re-engage quickly, is the hallmark of a trend that retains genuine conviction rather than momentum alone.\n\nThe structure story across the past month is straightforward. Price spent the better part of late June and early July consolidating in a tight band between 111.20 and 112.80, repeatedly testing the prior reaction zone near 111.21 before ultimately rejecting it with force. The breakout came on 14 July, when the daily candle pushed cleanly through 113.20 \u2014 itself now a well-established structure support with three recorded touches \u2014 and the pair has not looked back. The zone at 113.20 has effectively flipped from a ceiling into a floor in the market's mind, and the more proximate prior reaction zone at 114.33 has absorbed two intraday dips over the past week without producing a meaningful daily close beneath it. That level is the one to watch on any near-term softness.\n\nOn the H1 timeframe, the picture is constructive but consolidatory. After the early-morning push to 114.71 \u2014 the highest print in the current data set \u2014 price has drifted back toward the 114.44\u2013114.50 area and has essentially coiled there through the London morning. Hourly candles show progressively tighter ranges, wicks being absorbed, and no sustained downside follow-through. The 114.33 prior reaction zone sits roughly twelve pips below current price and represents the first meaningful area where intraday structure would need to hold to keep the short-term read intact.\n\nThe calendar brings the primary risk event: RBA Governor Bullock speaks at 23:05 UTC tonight. Given the AUD leg of this cross, her tone carries direct relevance. Any hawkish framing around the rate path \u2014 particularly if she pushes back against near-term easing expectations \u2014 could provide fresh impetus for AUD strength and extend the current leg higher. A notably dovish pivot or acknowledgement of deteriorating domestic conditions would represent the more disruptive scenario for the bullish read, potentially opening a test of the 114.33 zone and, if that gives way on a daily close basis, the 113.20 structure support further below.\n\nWhat would materially change the desk's bullish read is a daily close beneath 114.33, which would suggest the current consolidation has tipped into distribution rather than continuation. A move back through 113.20 on volume would call the entire post-July structure into question.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}